implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY (DoD 1, 2 and 3), once. From the task worktree root, run the checkRefs command exactly as written. Its fresh output, ending in GATE-OK, is moe.complete_task's verification evidence.

The command:
- fails if parseArgs, or the entry-guard block from `if (process.argv[1]` through its closing brace, differs from the fork point with moe/work-2026-10-24;
- archives HEAD (the daemon package, docs, scripts, CLAUDE.md and .gitignore) into /tmp and overlays your two working-tree files;
- under env -i, so no MOE_* var is set, runs `npm ci`, then `npx tsc -p . --noEmit` (vitest does not typecheck), then `npx vitest run src/commands/ src/index.version.test.ts`. That is DoD 3's exact suite; the new file lives in src/commands/.

At plan time this printed GATE-OK in about 8 s, with 5 files and 139 tests. With acea850b's index.ts the same command fails exactly cases 1, 2 and 6.
